    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bcf21d6_100bd4e8",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/SystemServiceManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-24T14:18:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When users load services from a platform jar (not an APEX one), it is possible that the classloader isn\u0027t created yet, unless the jar is listed in PRODUCT_STANDALONE_SYSTEM_SERVER_JARS. This can happen on downstream branches and in partners\u0027 codebases. Note that adding platform jars to the list is optional, and we don\u0027t have a plan to make it mandatory as the performance impact is minor and it may break things.\n\nI\u0027m fine with moving the check to SystemServerClassLoaderFactory, but I want to at least change the name here to remind users that this method has implications that a classloader may or may not be created, depending on some conditions.",
      "parentUuid": "81335b22_12585729",
